# RGJ-RC1-010L — direct MIDI/WAV Manager + PlatformPlayer facade integration
#
# Scope
# -----
# Completes the Java direct-media facade stage for the formats with a proven
# RG35XX backend: MIDI and WAV. Desktop/AWT behavior remains upstream-owned.
# ToneControl/vendor container conversion is intentionally a separate next stage
# and is not advertised by RG35XXMediaProfile until its JavaSound-free conversion
# path is source-audited.
#
# Exact upstream source basis
# ---------------------------
# - javax.microedition.media.Manager (TASEmulators/freej2me-plus devel)
# - org.recompile.mobile.PlatformPlayer (same devel tree)
# - org.recompile.mobile.JavaxPlatformPlayer extends PlatformPlayer and remains
#   the javax facade returned by Manager.
#
# Current upstream findings
# -------------------------
# Manager imports/owns desktop javax.sound.midi objects and createPlayer() returns
# JavaxPlatformPlayer. getSupportedContentTypes() advertises MIDI/WAV plus AMR,
# MPEG, MLD, MMF, iMelody and tone. playTone() directly uses JavaSound channels.
#
# PlatformPlayer imports JavaSound/sample/MPEG and its constructor immediately
# constructs midiPlayer/wavPlayer/MP3Player or sniff/decode variants. Therefore
# an RG35XX branch MUST happen before desktop backend construction for target
# direct formats.
#
# PART A — explicit target selector
# ---------------------------------
# `RG35XXPlatformProfile.isActive()` is the sole Java selector. It reads:
#   -Dfreej2me.rg35xx=true
# supplied by the RG35XX libretro process argv before `-jar`.
#
# The selector is independent from `freej2me.rg35xx.audio.fd`, because audio-FD
# creation may fail while the platform must still retain RG35XX-safe capability
# reporting/fail-safe behavior.
#
# Desktop/AWT launches without this property and remain on existing upstream
# JavaSound/MPEG paths.
#
# PART B — Manager capability gate
# --------------------------------
# In Manager.getSupportedContentTypes(protocol):
#
#   if(RG35XXPlatformProfile.isActive())
#       return RG35XXMediaProfile.getSupportedTypes(protocol);
#   else
#       return the existing upstream desktop list unchanged;
#
# RG35XX direct advertised types at this stage:
#   audio/midi
#   audio/x-midi
#   audio/wav
#   audio/x-wav
#
# Do NOT advertise audio/amr, audio/mpeg, audio/x-tone-seq, audio/mmf,
# audio/x-mld or audio/x-imy in this stage. Their direct target path is not yet
# fully proven.
#
# Manager.getSupportedProtocols(contentType) may preserve upstream behavior for
# desktop. On RG35XX it must not claim network/capture protocols; resource/input
# stream creation remains the primary path. Dedicated device locators are not
# evidence that audio/x-tone-seq conversion is complete.
#
# PART C — PlatformPlayer ownership
# ---------------------------------
# PlatformPlayer remains the public Player implementation and sole owner of:
# - javax.microedition.media.Player state surface
# - Control objects exposed to MIDP/vendor wrappers
# - PlayerListener + Siemens/KDDI/Nokia/DoJa/JBlend fan-out
# - public contentType semantics
#
# RG35XXNativePlayer remains a private backend/delegate. Do not make Manager
# return RG35XXNativePlayer directly and do not duplicate vendor callbacks.
#
# Add one optional field to PlatformPlayer:
#   private RG35XXNativePlayer rg35xxPlayer;
#
# Constructor ordering for InputStream/type:
#   1. initialize existing listener/control facade fields
#   2. if RG35XXPlatformProfile.isActive(), run the RG35XX direct-media path
#      BEFORE constructing midiPlayer/wavPlayer/MP3Player
#   3. otherwise execute existing upstream constructor unchanged
#
# PART D — RG35XX direct MIDI path
# --------------------------------
# If canonical type is MIDI:
#   rg35xxPlayer = new RG35XXNativePlayer(stream, canonicalType);
#   bind one reusable RG35XXMediaRegistry.EventListener that calls the existing
#   PlatformPlayer.notifyListeners() only after native registry drain
#   return from constructor without creating desktop midiPlayer/Sequencer/Synth
#
# If type is empty/unknown, bounded format sniffing may identify an MThd stream
# and route it here. Sniffing must read the stream exactly once into a byte array
# and recreate the backend from ByteArrayInputStream; do not rely on available()
# as complete stream length for arbitrary InputStream implementations.
#
# PART E — RG35XX WAV path
# ------------------------
# If canonical type is WAV, or bounded sniffing finds RIFF/WAVE:
#   1. decode via RG35XXWavDecoder.decode(...)
#   2. create RG35XXNativePlayer with WAV public content type
#   3. call setPcm16(decoded.pcm16, decoded.sampleRate, decoded.channels)
#   4. bind the same reusable native event listener
#   5. return before desktop AudioSystem/Clip construction
#
# WAV decoder/load allocations occur at realize/prefetch/setup time, not in the
# native render hot path.
#
# PART F — Player lifecycle delegation
# ------------------------------------
# Existing PlatformPlayer public methods keep their signatures and notification
# ownership. When rg35xxPlayer != null:
#
# realize():
#   rg35xxPlayer.realize(); facade state = REALIZED
#
# prefetch():
#   call rg35xxPlayer.prefetch(); on success facade state = PREFETCHED;
#   on failure remain REALIZED or throw MediaException according to the exact
#   upstream method signature/exception contract; never fall through and create
#   a desktop backend.
#
# start():
#   if rg35xxPlayer.start() succeeds, facade state = STARTED and call existing
#   notifyListeners(PlayerListener.STARTED, getMediaTime()) once.
#
# stop():
#   delegate STOP; facade state = PREFETCHED; preserve target STOP semantics
#   (media time resets to zero in native backend) and call STOPPED once.
#
# deallocate():
#   must not spawn the upstream JavaSound close threads for rg35xxPlayer.
#   Preserve semantic resource ownership without releasing the Player facade.
#
# close():
#   rg35xxPlayer.close(); facade state = CLOSED; existing CLOSED notification
#   behavior remains PlatformPlayer-owned.
#
# setMediaTime()/getMediaTime():
#   native media time is authoritative. PlatformPlayer forwards without Java
#   wall-clock timers.
#
# setLoopCount():
#   validate upstream MMAPI semantics then delegate exactly once. Native worker/
#   mixer owns actual loop decrement/restart.
#
# volumeControl:
#   preserve the existing facade Control object but delegate level changes to
#   RG35XXNativePlayer.setVolume().
#
# PART G — native event semantics correction
# ------------------------------------------
# `RG35XXMediaRegistry` and `RG35XXNativePlayer` were corrected in this stage:
# - EVENT_LOOPED is an intermediate restart and keeps started/STARTED state
# - EVENT_END_OF_MEDIA alone transitions to PREFETCHED/started=false
# - facade listener binding then calls existing notifyListeners(LOOPED/END,...)
#
# This prevents an intermediate LOOPED event from making PlatformPlayer appear
# stopped while native playback has already restarted.
#
# PART H — target unsupported direct types
# ----------------------------------------
# On RG35XX, unsupported direct AMR/MPEG/QCP/etc. must NOT fall through to
# desktop JavaSound/JLayer construction. Use the existing facade's unsupported/
# stub policy or throw MediaException where the exact upstream API expects it.
# Capability reporting must remain false.
#
# Java-side vendor decoders that can produce MIDI/WAV (MLD/MMF/iMelody/etc.) are
# deferred to the next conversion stage. They are not removed from desktop.
#
# PART I — target JVM property injection
# --------------------------------------
# The RG35XX libretro argv contract must include BOTH properties before -jar:
#   -Dfreej2me.rg35xx=true
#   -Dfreej2me.rg35xx.audio.fd=<fd>   (only when the dedicated pipe exists)
#
# The target selector property is always present for RG35XX even if the audio FD
# could not be created. This makes target safety/capability gating independent of
# transport availability.
#
# PART J — stage acceptance
# -------------------------
# STATIC-AUDIT-PASS for this direct-media facade stage requires:
# - explicit target selector; desktop remains unchanged
# - Manager advertised direct types exactly match proven backend types
# - PlatformPlayer branches before desktop MIDI/WAV backend creation
# - JavaxPlatformPlayer remains the javax facade
# - MIDI and WAV delegate to RG35XXNativePlayer/RG35XXWavDecoder
# - LOOPED keeps STARTED; END moves PREFETCHED
# - unsupported target types never instantiate desktop audio backends
# - no new Timer/executor/JavaSound requirement on RG35XX direct path
#
# BUILD-PASS remains blocked until this contract is applied to the assembled
# upstream Java sources and `rm -rf build && ant` succeeds.
